# Local, personal denylist for scripts/check_sensitive_content.py.
#
# Copy this file to .guardrails/local-denylist.txt (that exact filename is
# git-ignored - see .gitignore) and add exact strings specific to you or
# this AWS account that should never be committed: your real name, your
# AWS account ID, personal script/file paths, internal hostnames, etc.
#
# One literal string per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are
# ignored. Matching is exact-substring (case-sensitive), not regex - special
# characters in your entries are escaped automatically by the checker.
#
# This file (the .example one) is safe to commit since it has no real
# values. The real .guardrails/local-denylist.txt is never committed -
# that's the whole point: the values it protects never touch the repo,
# not even in this config file.
#
# Example entries (replace with your own):
# Jane Example
# 123456789012
# /opt/jane-personal-scripts/
